# Lucid model zoo: every registered model, from domain down to variant.
#
# How to read it
#   Domain > task or lineage > architecture > variants. The groups between the domain and the
#   architecture are a reading aid chosen by lineage; the code only has lucid/models/<domain>/<family>/.
#   Name [family] (N)   an architecture: [family] is its directory, N its registered model count.
#   a · b · c           the variants; prefix them with the family's name to get the factory.
#   b0 ~ b7             a range, ends included.
#   a × b               every combination of the two lists.
#   +cls, +gen, ...     each variant on that line also has that task wrapper (resnet_18_cls).
#   (note)              a remark, not a variant.
#
# Keeping it current (rule H12)
#   Adding, removing or renaming a family or a factory changes this file in the same commit.
#   `python -m tools.validate_model_zoo --runtime` fails if it disagrees with the registry:
#   every family must appear once, each count must match, each variant must exist, and each
#   group's total must add up. The registry stays the source of truth.

